x538 text "u32 is an exact 32-bit unsigned integer; every arithmetic result wraps modulo 2^32. bool is true or false, never a number. Arrays u32xN and records (T,T,...) are values: get, set, at, and put return a copy, they never alias. io is a linear token, meaning every io value is used exactly once; that is what makes output order checkable."
