x621 text "Views and edits"
x622 puts x620 x621
x623 call close x622 
x624 call open x623 2
x625 write x624 2
x626 text "A model never sees a whole file. It asks for a view of one function: the function with a handle line on top (e0), one signature line per callee, and a program handle (g0). The program view is scoped to the target, its transitive callees and its direct callers, so it stays the same size as the program grows. The revision is a short hash of the program text; an edit written against an older revision is rejected rather than applied to code that has moved. A reply is the handle line followed by edits, one per line, as in the quick start."
x627 puts x625 x626
x628 call close x627 
x629 call open x628 10
x630 write x629 4
